From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server, ntdll, win32u: BlockInput, key write times and transaction handles (3753)

server, ntdll, win32u: BlockInput, key write times and transaction handles

Three new server requests (a full rebuild of all unix modules): block_input
makes the desktop drop physical input and what other threads send, until the
blocking thread unblocks or ends (NtUserBlockInput, a new win32u syscall,
BlockInput); set_key_write_time lets NtSetInformationKey set the last write
time of a key; create_transaction and transaction_op make transactions real
handles that can be committed or rolled back once (NtCreateTransaction,
NtCommitTransaction, NtRollbackTransaction, ktmw32 asks for full access).

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto 5602 (stubs-6d) and 5203 (stubs-6c): transactions were implemented by 5602 (full server objects, NtOpenTransaction, query information, ktmw32 OpenTransaction) and by 3753; 5602's kept and 3753's create_transaction/transaction_op requests, server object (event.c, directory.c, object.h), ntdll sync.c and ktmw32 hunks dropped. 3753 keeps block_input (NtUserBlockInput) and set_key_write_time. server_protocol.h, request_handlers.h, request_trace.h (tools/make_requests) and win32syscalls.h (tools/make_specfiles, after 5203's syscalls) regenerated; protocol version 874.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/registry.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/registry.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/registry.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/registry.c
@@ -460,15 +460,23 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtSetInformationKey( HANDLE key, int class, void *info, ULONG le
 #endif
     if (!info) return STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION;
 
+    if (class == 0)  /* KeyWriteTimeInformation: needs KEY_SET_VALUE, the server checks the handle too */
+    {
+        const LARGE_INTEGER *time = info;
+
+        SERVER_START_REQ( set_key_write_time )
+        {
+            req->hkey = wine_server_obj_handle( key );
+            req->time = time->QuadPart;
+            ret = wine_server_call( req );
+        }
+        SERVER_END_REQ;
+        return ret;
+    }
+
     /* the handle has to be a valid key handle */
     ret = enumerate_key( key, -1, KeyCachedInformation, &cached, sizeof(cached), &dummy );
     if (ret && ret != STATUS_BUFFER_OVERFLOW) return ret;
-
-    if (class == 0)  /* KeyWriteTimeInformation needs server support */
-    {
-        FIXME( "KeyWriteTimeInformation not implemented\n" );
-        return STATUS_SUCCESS;
-    }
     /* the remaining classes only carry per-handle flags (WOW64 view, virtualization,
      * handle tags, layers) that have no observable effect in this registry */
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
